{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Recipe",
  "recipeCuisine": "Thailand",
  "name": "Deep Fried Soft Shell Crab",
  "text": "Deep Fried Soft Shell Crab\n\nPreparation time: 30 minutes\n\nCooking time: 2 minutes\n\nYield: 4\n\nIngredients\n\n8 frozen soft shell crab (defrosted),\n\n30 g cornflour,\n\n30 g plain flour,\n\nvegetable oil for frying,\n\n1 bunch spring onions (chopped),\n\n1 red chilli (finely sliced),\n\n2 cloves garlic (peeled),\n\n2 green birdseye chilies (sliced),\n\n1 tbsp kecap manis,\n\nsriracha chilli sauce.\n\nPreparation\n\nTo make the chilli salt\n\n1. Put 1 finely chopped red chilli and a peeled clove of garlic into a pestle and mortar.\n\n2. Gradually add the 4 tbsp of salt and pound the ingredients together.\n\n3. Pound until you have used up all the salt and are left with a pink paste with no pieces of chilli.\n\n4. Transfer the salt into a dish and put to the side.\n\nTo make the dipping sauce\n\n1. Finely slice your green birdseye chillies and place into a bowl.\n\n2. Add the juice of a lime and 1 clove of garlic, roughly chopped.\n\n3. Pour in 1 tbsp of kecap manis and give all the ingredients a good stir together.\n\nTo prepare the crabs\n\n1. Roughly chop up a bunch of spring onions and place into a dish.\n\n2. In a separate bowl mix together the cornflour and plain flour and then toss each of the crabs in the flour ensuring they are evenly coated.\n\n3. Heat your oil in a large wok and deep fry the crabs in batches for 2 minutes until golden brown and crispy.\n\n4. Drain thoroughly on kitchen paper.\n\nTo serve\n\n1. While the crabs are still warm and have just come out of the oil, sprinkle over a pinch of the chilli salt and the chopped spring onions.\n\n2.  Serve the crabs with the dipping sauce and some hot chilli sauce.",
  "prepTime": "PT30M",
  "cookTime": "PT2M",
  "recipeYield": "4",
  "recipeIngredient": [
    "8 frozen soft shell crab (defrosted),",
    "30 g cornflour,",
    "30 g plain flour,",
    "vegetable oil for frying,",
    "1 bunch spring onions (chopped),",
    "1 red chilli (finely sliced),",
    "2 cloves garlic (peeled),",
    "2 green birdseye chilies (sliced),",
    "1 tbsp kecap manis,",
    "sriracha chilli sauce."
  ],
  "recipeInstructions": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToSection",
      "name": "To make the chilli salt",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "1. Put 1 finely chopped red chilli and a peeled clove of garlic into a pestle and mortar."
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "2. Gradually add the 4 tbsp of salt and pound the ingredients together."
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "3. Pound until you have used up all the salt and are left with a pink paste with no pieces of chilli."
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "4. Transfer the salt into a dish and put to the side."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToSection",
      "name": "To make the dipping sauce",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "1. Finely slice your green birdseye chillies and place into a bowl."
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "2. Add the juice of a lime and 1 clove of garlic, roughly chopped."
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "3. Pour in 1 tbsp of kecap manis and give all the ingredients a good stir together."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToSection",
      "name": "To prepare the crabs",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "1. Roughly chop up a bunch of spring onions and place into a dish."
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "2. In a separate bowl mix together the cornflour and plain flour and then toss each of the crabs in the flour ensuring they are evenly coated."
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "3. Heat your oil in a large wok and deep fry the crabs in batches for 2 minutes until golden brown and crispy."
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "4. Drain thoroughly on kitchen paper."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToSection",
      "name": "To serve",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "1. While the crabs are still warm and have just come out of the oil, sprinkle over a pinch of the chilli salt and the chopped spring onions."
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "2.  Serve the crabs with the dipping sauce and some hot chilli sauce."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
